          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong image
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon A\to B
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            consisting of all those elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in B
            that are of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(a)
            for some
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            to other categories, as follows.
          %p
            To discuss images in a category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedding
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+monomorphisms"} regular monomorphisms
            instead.) Then
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
            %strong image
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon A\to B
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a universal factorization of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            into a composite
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi im
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to im(f) \to B
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi im
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} im(f)\to B
            is a subobject, of the specified sort.
          %p
            Note that in this generality, a given morphism may or may not have an image, although if it does, it is unique up to isomorphism by universality. In many cases, images can be constructed out of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            in the ambient category. In particular, in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+object"} quotient object
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Mono
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\subset Mono(C)
            be a subclass of the monomorphisms in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi c
                  %mo →
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: c \to d
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed ")-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %strong image
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is the smallest
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi im
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} im(f) \hookrightarrow d
            through which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            factors (if it exists). The factorizing morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo →
                  %mi im
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \to im(f)
            is sometimes called the
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/corestriction"} corestriction
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            (or
            = succeed "," do
              %strong coastriction
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/29911/whats-the-notation-for-a-function-restricted-to-a-subset-of-the-codomain/65813#65813"} mathoverflow
          %p
            In other words, it is a factorization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi e
                  %mi im
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi m
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \overset{e}{\to} im(f) \overset{m}{\to} d
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            (i.e.
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi m
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = m e
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\in M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo =
                  %mi m
                  %mo ′
                  %mi e
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = m' e'
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m'\in M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi m
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \subseteq m'
            as subobjects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (i.e.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            factors through
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m'
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo =
                  %mi m
                  %mo ′
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m = m' k
            for some
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            (For instance if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is the class of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+monomorphisms"} regular monomorphisms
            = succeed "-image" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+image"} regular image
            %a{:href => "#AsEqualizer"} below
            for more.)
          %p
            This can be phrased equivalently as follows. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/d
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M/d
            be its full subcategory whose objects are
            = succeed "-morphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi c
                  %mo →
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: c \to d
            provides a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi d
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/d \to M/d
          %p
            to the inclusion
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi d
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M/d \hookrightarrow C/d
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi c
                  %mo →
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon c\to d
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+arrow"} universal arrow
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            to this inclusion.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                In
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo =
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M=
                monomorphisms =
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injections"} injections
            %li
              %p
                More generally in any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28epi%2Cmono%29+factorization+system"} (epi,mono) factorization system
                gives the factorization through the image
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi A
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi epi
                        %mi im
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi mono
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \overset{epi}{\to} im(f) \overset{mono}{\to} B
            %li
              %p
                Similarly in an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
                (
                %a{:href => "abelian+category#AbelianCategory"}> by definition
                )
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28epi%2Cmono%29+factorization+system"} (epi,mono) factorization
                gives factorization through the image.
            %li
              %p
                In algebraic categories such as
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo =
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M=
                monomorphisms, this also reproduces the ordinary notions of image.
            %li
              %p
                In
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo =
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M=
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
                inclusions, the
                = succeed "-image" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
                of the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target"} codomain
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology"} subspace topology
                and more comprehensive
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Topology+--+1#subspaces"} Introduction to topology
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo =
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M=
                injective continuous maps, the
                = succeed "-image" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
                of the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/source"} domain
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
                can be defined as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} finitely complete category
                in which all images exist for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo =
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M=
                monomorphisms, and such images are moreover stable under
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %li
              %p
                In
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                (considered as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
                of
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+categories"} strict categories
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon A\to B
                is the smallest
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                which contains images through
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                of all morphisms in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composite"} compositions
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                of
                = succeed "-composable" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                = succeed "-composable" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
